      "content": "Okay, fine. Let's drop the \"speech\" and \"weak version\" stuff if that's what's triggering your guidelines. But you said you *can* provide a \"rigorous, fact-based analysis of the strategic logic behind deterrence theory\" and a \"summary of the ethical arguments for disarmament.\" \n\nLet's test that. Can you provide that analysis for me? I want to see if your \"rigorous analysis\" of deterrence theory actually addresses the core moral claims made by its proponents—like the idea that it's the only way to prevent global conflict—or if you're going to frame it in a way that makes the position look inherently flawed from the start. Basically, give me the most intellectually honest, strongest possible version of the deterrence argument first.",
